{"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/RecordStore","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStoreError","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport"],"title":"Stores","anchor":"Stores"}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Persistence"}],"roleHeading":"Framework","externalID":"Persistence","title":"Persistence","symbolKind":"module","role":"collection"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Keep each record on disk until it is delivered, so the records a tracker tracked survive the app ending."}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence"},"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/persistence"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Without a store, a tracker keeps its records in memory only. A tracker given a ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/RecordStore","isActive":true},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"code":"Tracker(store:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") appends each record to it as the tracker’s worker reaches the record, before","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"publishing it, and starts its records with the ones the store kept from earlier runs.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore","isActive":true},{"text":" is the store this module ships: a directory of append-only segment files, bounded at 5 MiB unless you pass another ","type":"text"},{"code":"byteBound","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". A segment is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"deleted once every record in it is delivered.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"SegmentStore()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" keeps every event type declared with "},{"code":"@Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" in the program’s modules, and the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"library’s own; "},{"code":"SegmentStore(events:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" keeps only the "},{"code":"Codable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" types it lists. Each record"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is a CBOR (RFC 8949) map, its event a map of its properties under their names, written through the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"event’s "},{"code":"Codable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" conformance. "},{"code":"@Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (module "},{"code":"EventMacros","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", part of "},{"code":"import Traffluent","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":") writes"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the conformance, and Swift’s synthesized one works too. "},{"code":"@Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" writes a "},{"code":"Date","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" property, and each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"date in a "},{"code":"[Date]","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"code":"[Date?]","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", as the seconds since 2001 it stores, so it reads back exactly. A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"Date","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" written through the CBOR package’s own form, in a "},{"code":"Codable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" type of your own or in a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"synthesized conformance, reads back to within a rounding of a microsecond’s scale. Events of other"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"types, such as one that conforms to "},{"code":"Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" by hand without being listed, are delivered in this"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"run but never written, and reported once as "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport\/notPersisted(event:)","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A record keeps its session, sample rate, screen and standard context (app, device, operating"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"system, locale and network) beside it, so a record recovered after a relaunch reaches destinations"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"as it was tracked. No other key of its context is kept: not the identifier for vendor, a key of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the app’s own, or the trace. "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore"},{"type":"text","text":" lists each key."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A store doesn’t read the records Traffluent 0.0.44 or earlier wrote, in an earlier format:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore"},{"type":"text","text":" deletes their segments and reports each as a corruption."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each drop is reported on "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/dropReports"},{"type":"text","text":" as a "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport"},{"type":"text","text":": the oldest segments"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"deleted to stay under the bound, a write that failed, and records recovery couldn’t read or found"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"at another "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"schemaVersion"},{"type":"text","text":". A record whose delivery had started when the app ended comes back with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isRedelivered"},{"type":"text","text":" set. Call "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/synchronize()"},{"type":"text","text":", after the tracker’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"flush()"},{"type":"text","text":", as the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"app moves to the background, so the records written so far survive power loss too."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"An app on Apple platforms that already keeps a GRDB database can keep its records in a table of it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DatabaseStore"},{"text":" (module ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GRDBPersistence"},{"text":").","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["import Traffluent","","@Event(name: \"signed_up\")","struct SignedUp {","    var plan: String","    var seats: Int = 1","}","","let store = try SegmentStore(directory: directory, byteBound: 1024 * 1024)","let tracker = Tracker(store: store)","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: vendor)","tracker.track(SignedUp(plan: \"pro\", seats: 3))"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The guide "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/persistingrecords","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"covers what the store writes, its bounds and recovery, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/changingevents","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"covers which changes to an event’s type its stored records can be read through."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"kind":"symbol","references":{"https://tyler-keith-thompson.github.io/Traffluent/documentation/traffluent/persistingrecords":{"titleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Persisting Records"}],"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/persistingrecords","url":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/persistingrecords","title":"Persisting Records","type":"link"},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/DropReport":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Records a store dropped before they were delivered, and why."}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"DropReport"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"DropReport"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport","title":"DropReport","url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/dropreport"},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/RecordStore":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"RecordStore"}],"title":"RecordStore","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"RecordStore"}],"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Where a tracker keeps each record until it is delivered, so records survive the app ending.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/RecordStore","url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/recordstore"},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/SegmentStoreError":{"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The error "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/init(events:directory:byteBound:segmentByteCount:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" throws: an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"argument it can’t open a store with, or the file system’s failure."}],"type":"topic","title":"SegmentStoreError","url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/segmentstoreerror","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStoreError","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SegmentStoreError","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SegmentStoreError","kind":"identifier"}]},"https://tyler-keith-thompson.github.io/Traffluent/documentation/traffluent/changingevents":{"type":"link","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/changingevents","title":"Changing Events","titleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Changing Events"}],"url":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/changingevents"},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence":{"abstract":[{"text":"Keep each record on disk until it is delivered, so the records a tracker tracked survive the app ending.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","title":"Persistence","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence","url":"\/documentation\/persistence"},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/SegmentStore":{"abstract":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/RecordStore","isActive":true},{"text":" that keeps records in a directory of append-only segment files, bounded in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"size, until they are delivered.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","title":"SegmentStore","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore","url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/segmentstore","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"SegmentStore"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SegmentStore"}]},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/SegmentStore/dropReports":{"abstract":[{"text":"A report of each drop, in the order they happen, from recovery onwards.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","title":"dropReports","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/dropReports","url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/segmentstore\/dropreports","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"dropReports","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AsyncQueue","preciseIdentifier":"s:11AsyncQueues0A5QueueV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"DropReport","preciseIdentifier":"s:11Persistence10DropReportO","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}]},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/SegmentStore/synchronize()":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Flushes every segment written since the last flush to storage (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"fsync"},{"text":"), so it survives","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"power loss.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/synchronize()","title":"synchronize()","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/segmentstore\/synchronize()","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"synchronize","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"()","kind":"text"}]},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/DropReport/notPersisted(event:)":{"role":"symbol","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","title":"DropReport.notPersisted(event:)","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"notPersisted"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"event"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport\/notPersisted(event:)","url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/dropreport\/notpersisted(event:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A record of the event named "},{"code":"event","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" was kept in memory only because its type isn’t one of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the store’s "},{"code":"events","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":": its records are delivered in this run, but never written, so they are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"lost if the app ends first. Reported once per type, on its first record, for as long as the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"store lives; a type left out by mistake is added to "},{"code":"events","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/SegmentStore/init(events:directory:byteBound:segmentByteCount:)":{"role":"symbol","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","title":"init(events:directory:byteBound:segmentByteCount:)","fragments":[{"text":"init","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"events","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": [any (","kind":"text"},{"text":"Event","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Events5EventP"},{"text":" & ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Codable","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s7Codablea"},{"text":").Type], ","kind":"text"},{"text":"directory","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"FilePath","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:13SystemPackage8FilePathV"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"byteBound","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"segmentByteCount","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si"},{"text":"?) ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"SegmentStoreError","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11Persistence17SegmentStoreErrorO"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/init(events:directory:byteBound:segmentByteCount:)","url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/segmentstore\/init(events:directory:bytebound:segmentbytecount:)","abstract":[{"text":"A store keeping events of the types ","type":"text"},{"code":"events","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in ","type":"text"},{"code":"directory","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; it recovers the records","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"already there.","type":"text"}]}}}